<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bachkovo Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1083</span> · Also known as Petritsoni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bachkovo Monastery, known in Georgian as Petritsoni, is an Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> monastery in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodope-mountains">Rhodope Mountains</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. It was founded in 1083 by Gregory Pakourianos, a Byzantine general of Georgian origin, for Georgian monks, and was a centre of Georgian learning where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioane-petritsi">Ioane Petritsi</a> worked. It later became one of the most important monasteries of the Bulgarian Orthodox Church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bachkovo-monastery.jpg" alt="Bachkovo Monastery" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kritzolina · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Church_of_the_Dormition,_Bachkovo_Monastery_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
